  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.1. Increased capacity of Member States to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2023, the Government of Zambia approved and launched the Capacity Building Booklet for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) Associations in Zambia to improve the enabling environment for the creation and growth of sustainable enterprises. This is in line with the Government&#x2019;s agenda to create robust indigenous entrepreneurship by promoting the growth and performance of Micro Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (MSMEs). The booklet has been developed to improve the operations of MSME Associations in the country because of full recognition that Small and Medium Business enterprises as key contributors to job and wealth creation, government allocated resources to the Zambia credit guarantee scheme. This has resulted into over 120 small and medium enterprises being supported with guarantees to enable them access financing from commercial banks, as well as supporting beneficiaries with Business Development Services using the Capacity Building Booklet for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME) Associations. With RBTC funding, in August 2022 the ILO held a high-level technical meeting with the Zambian Ministry of Small Medium and Enterprise Development (SMED). The ILO and the Ministry agreed to expedite the development and finalization of the SME Policy and the development of the Capacity Building Booklet for MSME Associations in Zambia other tools that the Ministry can utilize in executing its mandate to support MSME growth in the country</narrative>
   </description>
